# API Design Patterns

## Overview
REST and gRPC API design patterns, conventions, and best practices.

## REST API Conventions

### Endpoints
**✅ CORRECT - Use RESTful conventions:**
```typescript
@Controller('users')
export class UsersController {
  @Get() // GET /users
  async getUsers() {}
  
  @Get(':id') // GET /users/:id
  async getUser(@Param('id') id: string) {}
  
  @Post() // POST /users
  async createUser(@Body() dto: CreateUserDto) {}
  
  @Put(':id') // PUT /users/:id
  async updateUser(@Param('id') id: string, @Body() dto: UpdateUserDto) {}
  
  @Delete(':id') // DELETE /users/:id
  async deleteUser(@Param('id') id: string) {}
}
```

### Status Codes
- 200: Success
- 201: Created
- 400: Bad Request
- 401: Unauthorized
- 403: Forbidden
- 404: Not Found
- 500: Internal Server Error

### Pagination
**✅ CORRECT:**
```typescript
@Get()
async getUsers(@Query() query: PaginationDto) {
  const { page = 1, limit = 10 } = query;
  return {
    data: users,
    pagination: {
      page,
      limit,
      total,
      totalPages: Math.ceil(total / limit),
    },
  };
}
```

## gRPC Patterns

### Error Handling
**✅ CORRECT - Use RpcException:**
```typescript
import { RpcException } from '@nestjs/microservices';
import { GrpcStatusCode } from '@microservices-shared/grpc-exceptions';

@MessagePattern('getUser')
async getUser(data: { id: string }) {
  if (!data.id) {
    throw new RpcException({
      code: GrpcStatusCode.INVALID_ARGUMENT,
      message: 'User ID is required',
    });
  }
  // ...
}
```

**❌ WRONG - Never use HTTP exceptions in gRPC:**
```typescript
// ❌ WRONG
throw new BadRequestException('Invalid'); // Use RpcException instead
```

## Request/Response Validation
**✅ CORRECT - Validate DTOs:**
```typescript
import { IsString, IsEmail } from 'class-validator';

export class CreateUserDto {
  @IsString()
  @IsEmail()
  email: string;
}
```

